                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.12461/2610.12461v1/teaser.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:OuroWorld brings static 3D worlds alive.Left: Given a static 3DGS scene from any source, e.g., the 3D world models HY-World 2.0, Marble, and Lyra 2.0, OuroWorld converts it into a 3D cinemagraph: a dynamic scene with vivid, diverse motion that loops endlessly.Right: free-viewpoint renders along a moving camera, withgreen boxeshighlighting regions with noticeable dynamics.\nSmoke billows in the volcano (top), the galaxy scatters stardust (middle), and the ships bob up and down on the water (bottom).\nMotion stays consistent across viewpoints, and the scene att=Tt{=}Treturns tot=0t{=}0, so the loop is seamless.\nSee the supplementary videos for full results.",
                "position": 345
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "header": "1Introduction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.12461/2610.12461v1/motivation.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Motivation.Left:3D world models generate frozen worlds; 3D cinemagraphs bring them alive.Middle:Existing 3D cinemagraph methods rely on Eulerian flow and are limited to fluid-like motion.Right:We turn any static 3D scene into a 3D cinemagraph, which requires\n(1) seamless looping and (2) vivid, diverse dynamics.",
                "position": 356
            }
        ]
    },
